            <ArticleTitle>Technique for CT fluoroscopy-guided cervical interlaminar steroid injections.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>675-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2214/AJR.11.6809</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">We describe the use of CT fluoroscopy as a guidance tool for performing interlaminar epidural steroid injections in the cervical spine.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">CT fluoroscopy is an alternative method to perform cervical interlaminar steroid injections that allows precise needle placement in the epidural space.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
